.TH ORO-RUNTIME-INIT 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro\-runtime\-init \- embedder initialization and configuration helpers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <oro/runtime_init.h>
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The oro/runtime_init.h header exposes build\-time runtime metadata to host applications that embed Oro Runtime.
.PP
Callers can inspect embedded user configuration bytes, debug mode, development host settings, and the encoded configuration format without depending on internal runtime state.
.SH TYPES
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_user_config_format\fR
.nf
enum oro_runtime_user_config_format { ... } ;
.fi
.PP
Known user configuration formats returned by `oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_format()`.
.PP
Additional formats may be introduced over time; callers should handle unrecognized values by treating them as an opaque enum.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes\fR
.nf
const unsigned char* oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes (void);
.fi
.PP
Get a pointer to the embedded user configuration bytes, if any.
.PP
The buffer and its lifetime are owned by the runtime; callers must not free it. When no configuration is embedded this returns `NULL` and `oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes_size()` returns `0`.
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes_size\fR
.nf
unsigned int oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes_size (void);
.fi
.PP
Get the size in bytes of the buffer returned by `oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_bytes()`.
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_is_debug_enabled\fR
.nf
bool oro_runtime_init_is_debug_enabled (void);
.fi
.PP
Return `true` when the runtime was built in debug mode.
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_get_dev_host\fR
.nf
const char* oro_runtime_init_get_dev_host (void);
.fi
.PP
Get the development host configured for the embedded runtime, or an empty string when unset.
.PP
The returned pointer is owned by the runtime and remains valid for the lifetime of the process.
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_get_dev_port\fR
.nf
int oro_runtime_init_get_dev_port (void);
.fi
.PP
Get the development port configured for the embedded runtime, or `0` when unset.
.TP
\fBoro_runtime_init_get_user_config_format\fR
.nf
int oro_runtime_init_get_user_config_format (void);
.fi
.PP
Get the user configuration format as an integer value.
.PP
This corresponds to the `oro_runtime_user_config_format` enum above (for example, INI vs TOML). Callers should treat the value as an opaque enum and compare it against the symbolic constants rather than hard\-coding numeric literals.
.SH HEADER
include/oro/runtime_init.h
